# SPACBR — AUR packages
#
# Per §41-43 of CLAUDE.md: only add an entry when a specific, justified
# need can't be met officially, and note that justification next to
# it. The installer needs exactly one AUR helper (paru) to build
# these — don't add a second. paru itself is bootstrapped
# automatically (install_aur_helper in install/functions/packages.sh)
# if it isn't already present.
#
# arc-gtk-theme is NOT listed here even though it's an AUR package and
# SPACBR depends on it (every gtk-2.0/3.0/4.0 config and xinitrc's
# GTK_THEME assume Arc-Dark). It's built instead from
# packages/aur-overrides/arc-gtk-theme/, a SPACBR-maintained PKGBUILD
# fork -- verified for real that the published AUR PKGBUILD fails to
# build outright (hardcodes GNOME Shell 43 theming against a source
# tarball that doesn't have that asset layout). See that PKGBUILD's
# header for the full story, and the "GTK theme installed" doctor
# check in install/functions/checks.sh, which verifies
# /usr/share/themes/Arc-Dark actually exists on disk regardless of
# which path installed it.
#
# This file has no entries as a result. Add one here only for a
# plain, unmodified AUR package that doesn't need packages/aur-overrides
# treatment.

# --- Considered from your previous AUR list and deliberately left out ---
#
# clipmenu-git     — turned out clipmenu is an OFFICIAL package now
#                     (extra, last updated 2024-07-12) — see
#                     packages/desktop instead of here.
# yay-bin          — a second AUR helper. §43: at most one, and paru
#                     is already the one this installer uses.
# dust-git         — -git package (§42); a stable "dust" alternative
#                     may exist, check before adding.
# glow-git         — same -git issue as dust-git.
# ddgr-git         — same -git issue as dust-git.
# arc-icon-theme   — competes with the already-chosen Papirus-Dark
#                     icon set; Arc-Dark (the GTK *theme*) is kept,
#                     its matching icon set is not.
# brave-origin-nightly-bin, helium-browser-bin, zen-browser-bin
#                  — three more browsers; Firefox already owns
#                     "Browser" (§7). One owner per responsibility.
# session-desktop-bin, localsend-bin
#                  — messaging/file-transfer apps outside SPACBR's
#                     defined capability list (§44), same reasoning
#                     that already dropped the gajim keybinding.
# sublime-text-4   — competes with Neovim/Vim, the only editor owners
#                     CLAUDE.md §7 names.
# audacious-gtk3, audacious-plugins-gtk3
#                  — a dedicated music player; mpv already owns Media.
# topgrade-bin     — a general system-updater convenience wrapper,
#                     not a SPACBR responsibility; plain `pacman -Syu`
#                     plus `spacbr update` already cover this repo's
#                     actual needs.
